research/audit/wave5-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:30:{"id":"cex-unbounded-with-convergent-subsequence","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolzano%E2%80%93Weierstrass_theorem","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subsequence"],"rationale":"Positive novelty determination, on the witness. That the converse of Bolzano-Weierstrass fails is established (and is tagged as such on the false statement this item refutes, fs-convergent-subsequence-implies-bounded), but the WITNESS is bespoke: the interleaving 1, 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 4, ... defined by cases on the even/odd partition of N supplied by lem-alternating-sequence, together with the computation that its subsequential limit set is exactly {1}. No source selects this construction; the item builds it from this page's own machinery. That is the bespoke checkable-witness species the AUDIT-WORKFLOW sect. 6 trivial row assigns to ai-generated with generation.role: counterexample, on the wave-0 precedent Alpha upheld. Truth verified directly from the stated dependencies: the definition is total and single-valued because e and o partition N and each is injective; the subsequence along o is constantly 1, hence convergent; for any real M the Archimedean property gives m >= 1 with |M| < m, and y_{e_{m-1}} = m > |M| >= M, so no M bounds |y_n|; and any convergent subsequence meets the range of e only finitely often (its values j+1 exceed every bound), so it is eventually constantly 1 and its limit is 1, giving SL = {1}. Blast radius nil: zero deps consumers corpus-wide. Recorded for Alpha as a borderline - ai-altered under established-knowledge is defensible if Alpha judges the interleaving itself to be canonical.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-05"}
