items/cex-continuous-bijection-not-a-homeomorphism.md:89:- **The general pattern.** Any two comparable and distinct topologies on one set give such a witness, the identity from the finer to the coarser ([[fs-continuous-bijection-is-a-homeomorphism]]); the discrete topology is the finest of all ([[def-topological-space]]), so it pairs with every non-discrete topology on $\mathbb{R}$.
