items/lem-paracompact-hausdorff-is-regular.md:29:Every paracompact Hausdorff topological space is regular. No choice principle is
items/lem-paracompact-hausdorff-is-regular.md:34:**Given:** A paracompact Hausdorff space $X$, a closed set $F\subseteq X$, and a point $p\in X\setminus F$.
items/lem-paracompact-hausdorff-is-regular.md:36:[F1] Distinct points in a Hausdorff space have disjoint open neighbourhoods ([[def-hausdorff-space]]).
items/lem-paracompact-hausdorff-is-regular.md:48:1.1 For every $x\in F$, Hausdorffness gives disjoint open sets $U,V$ with $x\in U$ and $p\in V$; hence $p\notin\overline U$, since $X\setminus V$ is closed and contains $U$. Thus the family of all open $U$ with $U\cap F\ne\varnothing$ and $p\notin\overline U$, together with $X\setminus F$, is an open cover $\mathcal U$ of $X$. [F1, construct]
