items/lem-countably-compact-paracompact-hausdorff-is-compact.md:60:4.1 Hausdorffness makes points closed, so [L1] makes $D$ closed. For each $d\in D$, local finiteness gives a neighbourhood meeting only finitely many points of $D$; pass to an open subneighbourhood and remove those finitely many other closed points. Using [A1] along an enumeration of $D$ yields open sets $O_d$ with $O_d\cap D=\{d\}$. [A1, F3, L1, step 3.1, construct]
