research/audit/wave0-real-analysis-cauchy.provenance.jsonl:41:{"id":"lem-rat-inverse-well-defined","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ESCALATION-LEVEL NOTE for Alpha: well-definedness of the reciprocal [(a,b)]^-1 := [(b,a)] on Q \\ {0} is a standard step in every set-theoretic construction of Q (Landau, Tao Analysis I S4.2, Enderton Ch. 5), but no open source stating it as a named lemma surfaced. It is not an invented claim: it is the routine representative-independence obligation attached to the sourced reciprocal formula of Wikipedia Rational number, and is directly verifiable from def-rationals in one line (ab' = a'b <=> ba' = b'a by commutativity of Z). Recorded ai-altered/established-knowledge pending Alpha's independent concurrence. Local proof written here.\n\nALPHA CONCURS (2026-08-02). Representative-independence of the reciprocal on Q \\ {0} is a named, standard obligation in every set-theoretic construction of the rationals (Landau, Foundations of Analysis, Ch. 2; Enderton, Elements of Set Theory, Ch. 5; Tao, Analysis I, S4.2). The statement is the routine well-definedness clause attached to the sourced formula [(a,b)]^{-1} := [(b,a)], and it is recovered in one line from def-rationals by commutativity of multiplication in Z. Established standard knowledge; ai-altered under the D2 waiver, not ai-generated.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-02","alpha_reviewer":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)"}
research/audit/wave0-real-analysis-cauchy.provenance.jsonl:42:{"id":"lem-null-is-cauchy","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ESCALATION-LEVEL NOTE for Alpha: 'every convergent sequence is a Cauchy sequence' is bedrock textbook material, and this item is its limit-zero instance inside Q. No open page stating it in this exact rational-eps form surfaced, so no URL is claimed. It is certainly not invented: it is the standard implication specialised to null sequences. Recorded ai-altered/established-knowledge pending Alpha's independent concurrence. The three-step eps/2 proof is locally written.\n\nALPHA CONCURS (2026-08-02). \"Every convergent sequence is Cauchy\" is bedrock analysis (Rudin, Principles, 3.11(a); Tao, Analysis I, S6.1), and this item is exactly its limit-zero instance inside Q, with the standard eps/2 argument. Established standard knowledge; ai-altered under the D2 waiver, not ai-generated.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-02","alpha_reviewer":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)"}
research/audit/wave0-real-analysis-cauchy.provenance.jsonl:43:{"id":"ex-one-over-n-null","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ESCALATION-LEVEL NOTE for Alpha: '(1/n) is a null sequence' is the canonical first example of a sequence tending to zero and is the Archimedean property restated (Wikipedia Archimedean property already gives 'for all eps > 0 there is n in N with 1/n < eps'); no page presenting it as a worked EXAMPLE in this rational-only setting surfaced, so no URL is claimed for the example itself. Not invented. Recorded ai-altered/established-knowledge pending Alpha's independent concurrence; the three-line verification is locally written.\n\nALPHA CONCURS (2026-08-02). \"(1/n) tends to 0\" is the canonical first example of a null sequence and is a direct restatement of the Archimedean property, which the item cites as lem-rat-archimedean and which standard sources state in exactly the form \"for every eps > 0 there is n in N with 1/n < eps\". Established standard knowledge; ai-altered under the D2 waiver, not ai-generated.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-02","alpha_reviewer":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)"}
research/audit/wave0-linear-algebra.provenance.jsonl:23:{"id":"cex-pairwise-trivial-intersection-is-not-a-direct-sum","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ALPHA ESCALATION (evidence class needs concurrence). The proposition being witnessed is sourced: Axler 4e, remark after 1.46, 'When asking about a possible direct sum with more than two subspaces, it is not enough to test that each pair of the subspaces intersect only at 0', with Example 1.44 as its witness (three subspaces of F^3, pairwise intersections all {0}, sum all of F^3, decompositions not unique). No source was located for THIS witness, the three lines span{e_0}, span{e_1}, span{e_0 + e_1} in F^2. It is not an invention: it is the standard minimal separation (three distinct lines through the origin of a plane), it is recoverable directly from the sourced proposition by taking the smallest ambient space, and it is fully checkable in the two displayed decompositions of d. Recorded as ai-altered under the established-knowledge waiver rather than ai-generated; falls back to ai-generated if Alpha does not concur. Verification written locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}
research/audit/wave0-linear-algebra.provenance.jsonl:24:{"id":"ex-sum-and-intersection-in-f-three","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ALPHA ESCALATION (evidence class needs concurrence). The pair of coordinate hyperplanes U = {x : x_2 = 0} and W = {x : x_0 = 0} of F^3, with U + W = F^3 and U intersect W = span{e_1} so that the sum is not direct, is the standard 'a sum can be everything without being direct' computation; Axler 4e Examples 1.37, 1.42 and 1.44 are the same genus over F^3 (coordinate subspaces, their sums, and a non-direct sum), but no source was located for this exact pair of subspaces. It is a recoverable specialisation of established material, not an invented claim, and every assertion is verified by explicit coordinate computation in the item. Recorded as ai-altered under the established-knowledge waiver rather than ai-generated; falls back to ai-generated if Alpha does not concur. Verification written locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}
research/audit/wave0-linear-algebra.provenance.jsonl:26:{"id":"cex-pairwise-trivial-intersection-is-not-a-direct-sum","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ALPHA ESCALATION (evidence class needs concurrence). The proposition being witnessed is sourced: Axler 4e, remark after 1.46, 'When asking about a possible direct sum with more than two subspaces, it is not enough to test that each pair of the subspaces intersect only at 0', with Example 1.44 as its witness (three subspaces of F^3, pairwise intersections all {0}, sum all of F^3, decompositions not unique). No source was located for THIS witness, the three lines span{e_0}, span{e_1}, span{e_0 + e_1} in F^2. It is not an invention: it is the standard minimal separation (three distinct lines through the origin of a plane), it is recoverable directly from the sourced proposition by taking the smallest ambient space, and it is fully checkable in the two displayed decompositions of d. Recorded as ai-altered under the established-knowledge waiver rather than ai-generated; falls back to ai-generated if Alpha does not concur. Verification written locally.\n\nALPHA CONCURS (2026-08-02). The refuted proposition is sourced verbatim (Axler, Linear Algebra Done Right 4e, remark after 1.46: pairwise trivial intersection does not suffice for a direct sum of more than two subspaces). The witness, three distinct lines through the origin of a plane, is the canonical minimal separation and appears in essentially every treatment of internal direct sums with at least three summands; over the reals it is the familiar three-lines picture. This is a specialisation of established material to the smallest ambient space, and is fully checkable in the two displayed decompositions of d. Not AI-invented under the positive-determination standard; ai-altered under the D2 waiver.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-02","alpha_reviewer":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)"}
research/audit/wave0-linear-algebra.provenance.jsonl:27:{"id":"ex-sum-and-intersection-in-f-three","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ALPHA ESCALATION (evidence class needs concurrence). The pair of coordinate hyperplanes U = {x : x_2 = 0} and W = {x : x_0 = 0} of F^3, with U + W = F^3 and U intersect W = span{e_1} so that the sum is not direct, is the standard 'a sum can be everything without being direct' computation; Axler 4e Examples 1.37, 1.42 and 1.44 are the same genus over F^3 (coordinate subspaces, their sums, and a non-direct sum), but no source was located for this exact pair of subspaces. It is a recoverable specialisation of established material, not an invented claim, and every assertion is verified by explicit coordinate computation in the item. Recorded as ai-altered under the established-knowledge waiver rather than ai-generated; falls back to ai-generated if Alpha does not concur. Verification written locally.\n\nALPHA CONCURS (2026-08-02). Two coordinate hyperplanes of F^3 whose sum is F^3 and whose intersection is the remaining coordinate line is the standard \"a sum can be everything without being direct\" computation; Axler, Linear Algebra Done Right 4e, Examples 1.37/1.42/1.44 are the same construction over F^3. Every assertion in the item is verified by explicit coordinate computation. A recoverable specialisation of established material, not an invented claim; ai-altered under the D2 waiver.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-02","alpha_reviewer":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)"}
research/audit/wave5-topology-countability.provenance.jsonl:6:{"id":"lem-weight-is-well-defined","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://www1.essex.ac.uk/maths/people/fremlin/chap5a.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA for the evidence class. Fremlin 5A4A asserts the minimum defining w(X) by writing it down; no located source states its well-definedness as a separate proposition, because under AC it is immediate from 'every set has a cardinality' plus 'every nonempty set of ordinals has a least element'. This library splits it out so that def-weight-density-and-character / def-lindelof-degree-and-cellularity can discharge their justified_by obligations honestly. That is a recoverable restatement of established set theory, so under the positive-determination rule it is ai-altered and NOT ai-generated; recorded as established-knowledge pending Alpha's independent concurrence. The local proof is written from lem-ordinal-trichotomy and thm-well-ordering-theorem in the library's numbered-step format, hence ai-generated.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-05","escalated_to_alpha":true,"alpha_rationale":"Verified against the cited source directly (pdftotext of chap5a.pdf, 5A4A): Fremlin defines w(X) as \"the least cardinal of any base for T\" (a), d(X) as \"the smallest cardinal of any dense subset\" (c), c(X) as \"sup{#(G) : G subset of T\\{empty} is disjoint}\" (d), L(X) as \"the least cardinal kappa such that every open cover of X has a subcover with cardinal at most kappa\" (g)(i), and chi(x,X) as \"the smallest cardinal of any base of neighbourhoods of x\" with chi(X) = sup_x chi(x,X) (h). These match the library definitions exactly, including the RAW (un-normalized, no \"+omega\") convention that def-weight-density-and-character and def-lindelof-degree-and-cellularity declare. Fremlin writes each minimum/supremum down without proving it exists, exactly as Beta reported: the source presupposes well-definedness in a definition rather than stating it as a proposition. A definition that presupposes a least element is NOT a semantically identical statement of the proposition that the least element exists, so `semantic-source` would overclaim and `established-knowledge` is the honest class. ALPHA CONCURS that the statement is standard established mathematics: under AC every set has a cardinality, the relevant families are sets (subfamilies of the topology, subsets of X), so the cardinalities form a nonempty set of cardinals, which has a least member and a set-sized supremum. This is routine set-theoretic topology (Juhasz, Cardinal Functions in Topology; Engelking, General Topology) and carries no positive indication of AI novelty, so the positive-determination standard forbids `ai-generated`. Statement stays `ai-altered`. SCOPE OF THIS CONCURRENCE: it certifies the STATEMENT as standard. It is not a proof certification — proof provenance stays `ai-generated` and these items remain in the A6 CRITICAL refuter set.","alpha_at":"2026-08-05"}
