+# Wave 7 topology-uniform Audit-Beta findings
+
+## Continuity checkpoint — 2026-08-08
+
+- Current substage: A1 provenance research and A2 proof/citation audit are in progress; A4 has not begun because no A3 approval has been issued.
+- Owned artifacts: `research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl`, `research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.findings.md`, and `research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json`; only this findings file exists so far.
+- Verified scope: the manifest contains the `uniform-spaces` A page with 54 in-scope items and the `uniform-spaces-examples` B page with 7 in-scope items: 61 items total, of which 45 contain numbered proofs or verifications. The already dual-tagged `ex-uncountable-cantor-cube-uniformizable-not-first-countable` is excluded and will not be audited or ledgered.
+- Completed checks: `CLAUDE.md`, `research/audit/RESUME.md`, `AUDIT-WORKFLOW.md`, `QUALITY-CONTROLS.md`, `SCHEMA.md`, the split/manifest/run-state files, both page files, all 61 in-scope item files, and their 54 distinct on-disk dependency targets have been read. The principal arguments have been checked once; proof-contract transcription and a systematic second pass over every fact citation remain open.
+- Open mathematical constraints: provenance labels must distinguish exact or semantic matches from merely related literature, especially where the published statement makes explicit ZF, DC, or ultrafilter-lemma assumptions. No unsourced standard result may be entered as `ai-altered`/`established-knowledge` without Alpha concurrence, and no item may be called `ai-generated` merely because a search failed.
+- Concrete defects found so far: the library's proper-filter convention makes every uniform space nonempty, but empty metric spaces, empty completely regular spaces, and empty compact Hausdorff spaces are admitted. Consequently the published metric/gauge/cover dictionary and the uniformizable/completely-regular and compact-Hausdorff uniqueness chain contain unqualified empty-carrier failures. Separately, `lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base` is repeatedly cited for square roots and arbitrary finite-composite control absent from its Statement; the minimal-Cauchy-filter construction never establishes that its carrier is nonempty before generating a proper uniformity; `ex-r-and-open-interval-homeomorphic-not-uniformly-isomorphic` attributes a triangle-inequality consequence to `lem-of-abs-value`, whose Statement contains no triangle inequality; and `thm-complete-and-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-compact` cites `thm-ultrafilter-lemma`, whose Statement assumes full Choice, even though `thm-compactness-via-nets-filters-and-ultrafilters` alone states the required ultrafilter-lemma compactness criterion.
+- Exact next action: finish the eight-case boundary sweep through every construction, settle the smallest coupled repair set for A3, then encode all 45 proof contracts and finish the source-backed provenance classifications.
