const W='https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf';
const E='https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space';
const V='https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf';
const B='https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf';
const R='https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~rosendal/PapersWebsite/Coarse-Geometry-Book23.pdf';
const K='https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-31.pdf';
const C='https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Complete_uniform_space';
const H='https://www.boletin.math.org.mx/pdf/2/34/BSMM%282%29.34.11-21.pdf';
const rows=[
['def-uniform-space-by-entourages','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,E],'not-applicable','Wodzicki Definition 2.1 and Encyclopedia of Mathematics U1-U3 state the same proper-filter entourage axioms, quantifiers, and directions; only notation changes.'],
['lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base','literature-derived','exact-source',[W],'ai-altered','Wodzicki states that the symmetric entourages form a base. The published proof is a rewritten intersection-with-inverse argument. The finite-composite strengthening proposed at A3 is also Wodzicki Exercise 23, but is absent from the current Statement.'],
['thm-uniformity-induces-a-topology','literature-derived','exact-source',[W],'ai-altered','Wodzicki defines the uniform topology by exactly the entourage-ball neighborhood condition and proves it is a topology; the item changes notation only.'],
['def-separated-uniform-space','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,E],'not-applicable','Both sources define separatedness by the intersection of all entourages being the diagonal, with the same convention and no changed hypothesis.'],
['thm-separated-uniformity-iff-induced-topology-is-hausdorff','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,E],'ai-altered','The sources state the same biconditional for the topology induced by an entourage uniformity. The local proof expands the two directions.'],
['def-uniformly-continuous-map','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,B],'not-applicable','Wodzicki Definition 4.6 and the BIU notes give the same entourage pullback quantifiers for uniform continuity.'],
['thm-uniformly-continuous-maps-are-continuous','literature-derived','exact-source',[W],'ai-altered','Wodzicki states exactly that a uniformly continuous map is continuous in the respective uniform topologies; the item supplies the standard ball proof.'],
['lem-metric-uniformity-dictionary','ai-altered','semantic-source',[W,B],'ai-altered','The sources give the metric entourages, induced metric topology, separation, and the epsilon-delta interpretation. The item packages these clauses and, unlike the source convention, the library permits an empty metric carrier while requiring filters proper; this creates the empty-carrier defect escalated in A3.'],
['def-uniform-cover-space','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,W],'not-applicable','Encyclopedia of Mathematics gives the uniform-cover axioms and Wodzicki develops the associated cover relation. The item uses an equivalent star-refinement presentation and currently overstates equivalence on the empty carrier under the library proper-filter convention.'],
['lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,W],'ai-altered','The sources give the standard equivalence between entourage and uniform-cover formulations. The item spells out both constructions; its cover-to-entourage direction needs the nonempty-carrier qualification recorded for A3.'],
['def-gauge-of-pseudometrics','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,V,B],'not-applicable','The sources define a uniformity from finite intersections of pseudometric balls. The item calls the family a gauge and bundles topology and uniform-continuity clauses; under the local proper-filter convention it also needs a nonempty carrier.'],
['lem-normal-sequences-of-entourages','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[W,V],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Iterated symmetric entourage roots are the standard normal-sequence construction in both sources, but the published Statement makes the strictly weaker foundational hypothesis DC explicit and no located source states that same choice-calibrated proposition. It is established construction, not novel; the recursion proof is local.'],
['lem-pseudometric-from-a-normal-entourage-sequence','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,V],'ai-altered','Both sources state the normal-sequence metrization lemma with the same dyadic control inclusions and path-infimum pseudometric construction. The proof is a notation-adjusted expansion of that argument.'],
['thm-entourage-uniformities-are-generated-by-gauges','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[W,V],'ai-altered','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The sources prove every uniformity is generated by pseudometrics, but assume an ordinary classical background; the item isolates DC as sufficient. The mathematical theorem is standard, but no source with the same foundational hypothesis surfaced.'],
['thm-three-definitions-of-uniform-space-are-equivalent','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[E,W,V],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Literature gives the entourage-cover equivalence and pseudometric generation, but not this exact compound ZF/DC calibration. This is a standard synthesis, not an invented theorem; the local proof composes the preceding dictionary and gauge results.'],
['def-cauchy-filter-in-a-uniform-space','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,E],'not-applicable','The sources use the same requirement that for every entourage a filter member have square contained in it; notation and the equivalent uniform-cover wording are the only differences.'],
['lem-convergent-filters-are-cauchy','literature-derived','exact-source',[W],'ai-altered','Wodzicki Exercise 41 states exactly that every filter convergent in the uniform topology is Cauchy. The item supplies the standard symmetric-root proof, with a missing direct citation proposed at A3.'],
['lem-cauchy-filter-with-a-cluster-point-converges','literature-derived','exact-source',[W],'ai-altered','Wodzicki Exercise 45 states that every adherence point of a Cauchy filter is its convergence point. The local proof expands this and needs the induced-topology citation recorded at A3.'],
['def-complete-uniform-space','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,C],'not-applicable','Both sources define a complete uniform space as one in which every Cauchy filter converges, exactly as the item does.'],
['def-uniform-embedding-and-uniform-isomorphism','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,W],'not-applicable','The literature uses the same uniform-isomorphism and subspace-uniformity notions. The item packages the embedding and isomorphism definitions in library notation.'],
['def-completion-of-a-uniform-space','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,W,C],'not-applicable','The sources define completion by a complete separated target with dense canonical image and induced original uniformity. The item explicitly permits a noninjective Hausdorff reflection map, an equivalent convention for nonseparated inputs.'],
['lem-minimal-cauchy-filter-associated-to-a-cauchy-filter','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,H],'ai-altered','Wodzicki 6.1.2-6.1.5 and Hunt give the canonical unique minimal Cauchy filter contained in a Cauchy filter. The current proof follows this construction; A3 proposes stating the sourced principal-filter clause needed downstream.'],
['lem-entourages-on-minimal-cauchy-filters-form-a-separated-uniformity','ai-altered','semantic-source',[W,H],'ai-altered','Wodzicki restricts the standard filter-base uniformity to minimal Cauchy filters and states it is Hausdorff. The item spells out the entourage relation. Its proof omits the nonempty-carrier discharge, which the sourced principal-filter clause supplies.'],
['lem-minimal-cauchy-filter-space-is-complete','ai-altered','semantic-source',[W,H],'ai-altered','The sources construct the completion from minimal Cauchy filters; completeness of that space is part of the construction. The item isolates and expands that component as a lemma.'],
['lem-point-filters-are-dense-in-the-minimal-cauchy-filter-space','ai-altered','semantic-source',[W,H],'ai-altered','Wodzicki 6.1.6-6.2.4 gives the point-neighborhood-filter map, uniform continuity, and density. The item packages these conclusions; A3 proposes adding the member-contains-the-point clause actually used later.'],
['thm-hausdorff-completion-of-a-uniform-space','ai-altered','semantic-source',[W,E,C],'ai-altered','The sources state existence of a dense complete Hausdorff completion; Wodzicki also identifies when the canonical map reflects the original uniformity. The item packages the Hausdorff reflection and embedding criterion.'],
['thm-uniform-completion-universal-property-and-uniqueness','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,E],'ai-altered','Wodzicki 6.2.3 states the same unique extension of every uniformly continuous map into a complete Hausdorff uniform space. Uniqueness of completions is the exact categorical consequence; the local proof expands it.'],
['def-totally-bounded-uniform-space','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,W],'not-applicable','Encyclopedia of Mathematics defines precompactness by finite uniform-cover refinement, equivalently finitely many entourage balls. The item adopts the standard name totally bounded and the entourage formulation.'],
['lem-ultrafilters-on-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-cauchy','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E],'ai-generated','The standard compactness/precompactness filter characterization in Encyclopedia of Mathematics entails the same ultrafilter lemma. The item isolates the elementary finite-cover proof.'],
['lem-compact-uniform-spaces-are-complete','literature-derived','exact-source',[E,C],'ai-altered','The sources state that compact uniform spaces are complete, with the same filter notion. The local proof uses compactness through cluster points.'],
['lem-compact-uniform-spaces-are-totally-bounded','literature-derived','exact-source',[E],'ai-altered','Encyclopedia of Mathematics gives compactness of a uniform space only with precompactness and completeness and identifies precompactness with finite uniform coverings; this direction is exactly the item claim.'],
['thm-complete-and-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-compact','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[E],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The implication is the standard complete-plus-precompact compactness theorem, but the item explicitly assumes only the ultrafilter lemma, whereas the located source works classically. The local ultrafilter proof verifies that weaker assumption; the extra full-Choice citation is an A3 citation defect.'],
['cor-uniform-compactness-equivalence','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[E],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Compact iff complete and totally bounded is standard and appears in the literature, but the item records the precise ultrafilter-lemma assumption for the reverse implication. No located source states that same foundational calibration.'],
['lem-finite-star-refinement-for-compact-hausdorff-spaces','ai-altered','semantic-source',[W,V],'ai-altered','The compact-Hausdorff uniformization proofs in the sources construct finite open refinements with the required star control. The item extracts that standard construction as a named lemma and writes its finite cover argument explicitly.'],
['thm-compact-hausdorff-open-cover-uniformity','ai-altered','semantic-source',[W,V],'ai-altered','The sources construct the unique compatible uniformity on a compact Hausdorff space from diagonal neighborhoods/open covers. The item uses the equivalent uniform-cover formulation. Its final entourage-recovery step fails only for the locally admitted empty compact space and is escalated.'],
['thm-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-unique-compatible-uniformity','ai-altered','semantic-source',[W,V],'ai-altered','Vienna Theorem 9.4.14 and Wodzicki Corollary 4.8 give uniqueness, with Vienna also giving existence, for the standard nonempty convention. The library admits the empty compact Hausdorff space but no uniformity on it, so the current exactly-one claim needs a nonempty hypothesis.'],
['cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous','ai-altered','semantic-source',[W,B],'ai-altered','Wodzicki Theorem 4.7 and the BIU notes state the compact-domain uniform-continuity theorem for the natural compatible uniformity. The library empty-space convention requires a nonempty domain, and the proof also needs the cover dictionary cited explicitly.'],
['def-countably-based-uniformity','literature-derived','exact-source',[B,V],'not-applicable','The sources define a uniform base by cofinal refinement and countable base exactly as the item does.'],
['lem-countable-uniform-base-normalisation','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[V],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Decreasing symmetric bases with triple-composite control are the standard metrization normalization, but the item emphasizes that its explicit finite-intersection recursion works in ZF. No located source states this exact choice-free proposition.'],
['thm-countably-based-uniformity-is-pseudometrizable','ai-altered','semantic-source',[V,B],'ai-altered','The sources give pseudometrizability of countably based uniformities and the separated/Hausdorff criterion for the pseudometric to separate points. The item packages both clauses. Its metric criterion needs a direct metric-definition citation.'],
['def-uniformizable-space','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,V],'not-applicable','Wodzicki and Vienna define uniformizable as having a compatible uniformity; the item additionally names the standard separated variant without altering either definition.'],
['lem-uniformizable-spaces-are-regular','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,V],'ai-altered','The sources state the regularity consequence of a compatible uniformity with the same non-T1 convention used by the item. The local proof is the standard entourage-shrinking argument.'],
['lem-uniformizable-spaces-are-completely-regular','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[V,B],'ai-altered','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Literature proves uniformizable spaces completely regular via pseudometrics, but the item makes DC explicit as the only construction principle. No source with that same foundational hypothesis surfaced.'],
['lem-completely-regular-topologies-come-from-continuous-pseudometrics','ai-altered','semantic-source',[V,B],'ai-altered','Vienna Theorem 9.4.15 and the BIU pseudometric construction use the continuous functions p_f(x,y)=|f(x)-f(y)| to recover the topology. The item makes the gauge explicit; its empty-carrier and triangle-inequality citation defects are escalated.'],
['thm-uniformizable-iff-completely-regular','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[V,B],'ai-altered','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The uniformization theorem is standard, but the published biconditional asserts DC suffices and the local definition admits the empty completely regular space while proper filters exclude it. No source matches both conventions and foundational hypothesis; a nonempty repair is proposed.'],
['cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[V,B],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The separated version of the uniformization theorem is standard, but the item exposes DC and uses the library Tychonoff convention. The empty carrier is currently a counterexample, and the T1/Hausdorff bridge citations are incomplete.'],
['def-topological-group','literature-derived','exact-source',[B],'not-applicable','The BIU notes define a topological group by continuity of multiplication and inversion, exactly matching the item.'],
['lem-topological-group-translations-and-inversion','literature-derived','exact-source',[B],'ai-altered','The BIU notes state that left/right shifts and inversion are homeomorphisms. The local proof expands continuity and inverse formulas.'],
['def-left-and-right-uniformities-of-a-topological-group','literature-derived','exact-source',[B],'not-applicable','BIU Example 8.6 gives exactly the left and right basic entourages x"'^{-1}y in U and xy''^{-1} in U, up to naming orientation.'"'],
['thm-topological-group-uniformities-induce-the-given-topology','ai-altered','semantic-source',[B],'ai-altered','The BIU notes state that the natural group uniformities induce the group topology and give their formulas. The item additionally spells out inversion as a uniform isomorphism between them.'],
['def-upper-and-roelcke-uniformities-of-a-topological-group','literature-derived','exact-source',[B,R],'not-applicable','BIU Remark 8.7 defines the upper uniformity as the join and Roelcke as the meet; Rosendal Definition 3.1 gives the same meet and VxV basic entourages.'],
['cor-topological-groups-are-completely-regular','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[B,V],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Uniformizability of every topological group and complete regularity of uniformizable spaces are standard, but the item states the precise DC-dependent composition under the library non-Hausdorff convention. No source states that exact package.'],
['def-pointwise-and-uniform-convergence-uniformities','ai-altered','semantic-source',[B],'not-applicable','BIU defines pointwise convergence from finite coordinate restrictions and uniform convergence from the full coordinate set. The item writes explicit bases P(F,V) and Q(V), an equivalent notation.'],
['lem-uniform-convergence-uniformity-is-finer-than-pointwise','ai-altered','semantic-source',[B],'ai-generated','BIU gives the two bases. Their inclusion and equality when the domain itself is finite are the immediate standard comparison isolated by this item.'],
['ex-usual-metric-uniformity-on-r','ai-altered','semantic-source',[W,B],'ai-generated','The metric-uniformity construction in both sources specializes to the usual absolute-value metric on R and gives its usual topology and epsilon-delta uniform continuity. The item is that standard specialization.'],
['ex-r-and-open-interval-homeomorphic-not-uniformly-isomorphic','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The homeomorphism h(x)=x/(1+|x|) and its inverse are a standard bounded-coordinate example; targeted searches found only informal exact discussions, not an allowed reputable source for this precise witness. The displayed estimates verify it, so it is established rather than positively novel. A triangle-inequality citation is nevertheless wrong and is proposed for repair.'],
['fs-a-compatible-uniformity-is-unique','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[W],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Nonuniqueness of compatible uniformities on noncompact spaces is standard; Wodzicki proves uniqueness only in the compact case and supplies standard continuous-not-uniformly-continuous witnesses. No source states this exact false universal plus the item\\'s pullback refutation.'],
['ex-additive-group-uniformity-on-r','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[B,R],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The group-uniformity formulas are sourced and commutativity immediately makes left, right, upper, and Roelcke coincide with the usual metric uniformity on additive R. No located source states this exact four-way worked example, but it is standard, not novel.'],
['ex-pointwise-but-not-uniform-convergence-on-a-countable-domain','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Moving-tail indicator functions are a canonical pointwise-not-uniform convergence witness, but no reputable source with this exact N-to-{0,1} construction surfaced. The verification is direct and shows established mathematics, not novelty; the discrete-uniformity citation is incomplete.'],
['ex-closed-unit-interval-has-one-compatible-uniformity','ai-altered','semantic-source',[V,W],'ai-generated','Vienna Theorem 9.4.14 gives the unique compatible uniformity on every compact Hausdorff space, and the metric construction identifies it on [0,1]. The item is the standard closed-interval specialization.'],
['cex-k-topology-is-not-uniformizable','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[K,V],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The ETSU Munkres notes prove that the K-topology is Hausdorff but not regular, while the uniformization theorem says uniformizable spaces are regular. Their composition gives the item exactly, but no located source states the resulting nonuniformizability as a single proposition; it is standard and not novel.']
];
