+          "id": "step-1.3",
+          "claim": "Conversely, let $\\mathcal O$ be an open cover and take a finite open star-refinement $\\mathcal W$ by [L5]. Form the family of all open sets $N$ for which there are $x\\in N$, $W\\in\\mathcal W$, and a symmetric entourage $D$ satisfying $N\\subseteq D[x]$ and $D^{\\circ2}[x]\\subseteq W$. This family covers $X$: given $x$, first take $W\\in\\mathcal W$ containing it, then use compatibility and a symmetric square root to obtain such $D$ and an open neighbourhood $N\\subseteq D[x]$. Compactness gives finitely many witnesses $(N_i,x_i,W_i,D_i)$ covering $X$. Put $D=\\bigcap_iD_i$. If $y\\in N_i$ and $z\\in D[y]$, then symmetry gives $x_iD_i yD_i z$, so $z\\in D_i^{\\circ2}[x_i]\\subseteq W_i$. Hence the $D$-ball cover refines $\\mathcal W$, and therefore refines $\\mathcal O$. Thus every open cover is uniform for $\\mathcal U$. [L3, L4, L5, choose]",
