+          "quote": "Let $P$ be a property of naturals such that for every $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$, if $P(m)$ holds for all $m < n$ then $P(n)$. Then $P(n)$ holds for all $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$. (At $n = 0$ the hypothesis is vacuous, so $P(0)$ is forced.)",
