+{"id":"lem-normal-sequences-of-entourages","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Iterated symmetric entourage roots are the standard normal-sequence construction in both sources, but the Statement makes the strictly weaker foundational hypothesis DC explicit and no located source states that same choice-calibrated proposition. It is established, not novel; the recursion proof is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"lem-pseudometric-from-a-normal-entourage-sequence","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"Both sources state the normal-sequence metrization lemma with the same dyadic control inclusions and path-infimum pseudometric construction. The proof is a notation-adjusted expansion.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"thm-entourage-uniformities-are-generated-by-gauges","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The sources prove every uniformity is generated by pseudometrics but assume an ordinary classical background; the item isolates DC as sufficient. The theorem is standard, but no source with the same foundational hypothesis surfaced.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"thm-three-definitions-of-uniform-space-are-equivalent","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Literature gives the entourage-cover equivalence and pseudometric generation, but not this exact compound ZF/DC calibration. This is a standard synthesis, not an invented theorem; the proof composes the preceding results.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"def-cauchy-filter-in-a-uniform-space","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"The sources use the same requirement that for every entourage a filter member have square contained in it; notation and equivalent cover wording are the only differences.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
