### def-uniform-cover-space
## Definition

For a cover $\mathcal V$ of $X$ and $A\subseteq X$, write $\operatorname{St}(A,\mathcal V)$ for the union of the members of $\mathcal V$ meeting $A$. A cover $\mathcal V$ **star-refines** $\mathcal W$ if for every $V\in\mathcal V$, $\operatorname{St}(V,\mathcal V)$ is contained in some member of $\mathcal W$.

### lem-metric-uniformity-dictionary
## Statement

For a metric space $(X,d)$, the sets $E_\varepsilon=\{(x,y):d(x,y)<\varepsilon\}$, $\varepsilon>0$, generate a separated uniformity. Its induced topology is the metric topology, and uniform continuity to another metric uniformity is exactly metric uniform continuity.

### lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary
## Statement

In ZF, an entourage uniformity determines a uniform-cover structure by the covers $\{E[x]:x\in X\}$, and a uniform-cover structure determines an entourage uniformity by the sets $\bigcup_{V\in\mathcal V}V\times V$. These constructions recover the same uniform structure.

### def-gauge-of-pseudometrics
## Definition

A **gauge of pseudometrics** on $X$ is a family $\mathcal P$ of pseudometrics ([[def-metric-space]]). For finite $F\subseteq\mathcal P$ and $\varepsilon>0$, put $E(F,\varepsilon)=\{(x,y):p(x,y)<\varepsilon\text{ for every }p\in F\}$. The nonempty such sets form a filter base and generate a uniformity ([[def-filter-base]], [[lem-filter-base-generates]]), called the uniformity **generated by $\mathcal P$**.

For an already given uniformity $\mathcal U$ on $X$, a pseudometric $p$ is
**uniformly continuous for $\mathcal U$** when
$$
\{(x,y):p(x,y)<\varepsilon\}\in\mathcal U
$$
for every $\varepsilon>0$. With this terminology, each member of a gauge is
### thm-three-definitions-of-uniform-space-are-equivalent
## Statement

In ZF, the entourage and uniform-cover formulations determine each other. Assuming dependent choice, they are also equivalent to the formulation by gauges of pseudometrics.

### lem-completely-regular-topologies-come-from-continuous-pseudometrics
## Statement

The topology of a completely regular space is induced by the gauge of pseudometrics $p_f(x,y)=|f(x)-f(y)|$, where $f:X\to[0,1]$ ranges over continuous maps.

### thm-uniformizable-iff-completely-regular
## Statement

**Assuming dependent choice,** a topological space is uniformizable if and only if it is completely regular.

### cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff
## Statement

**Assuming dependent choice,** a topological space is separated-uniformizable if and only if it is Tychonoff.

### thm-compact-hausdorff-open-cover-uniformity
## Statement

For a compact Hausdorff space, the covers that admit an open refinement form a compatible uniform-cover structure. In particular every open cover is uniform.

### thm-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-unique-compatible-uniformity
## Statement

A compact Hausdorff topology carries exactly one compatible uniformity.

### cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous
## Statement

Every continuous map from a compact Hausdorff space to a uniform space is uniformly continuous.


