+{"id":"def-uniform-space-by-entourages","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"Wodzicki Definition 2.1 and Encyclopedia of Mathematics U1-U3 state the same proper-filter entourage axioms, quantifiers, and directions; only notation changes.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki states that symmetric entourages form a base. The proof is a rewritten intersection-with-inverse argument. The finite-composite strengthening proposed at A3 is also Wodzicki Exercise 23 but is absent from the current Statement.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"thm-uniformity-induces-a-topology","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki defines the uniform topology by exactly the entourage-ball neighborhood condition and proves it is a topology; the item changes notation only.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"def-separated-uniform-space","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"Both sources define separatedness by the intersection of all entourages being the diagonal, with the same convention and no changed hypothesis.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"thm-separated-uniformity-iff-induced-topology-is-hausdorff","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"The sources state the same biconditional for the topology induced by an entourage uniformity. The local proof expands the two directions.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"def-uniformly-continuous-map","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki Definition 4.6 and the BIU notes give the same entourage pullback quantifiers for uniform continuity.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"thm-uniformly-continuous-maps-are-continuous","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki states exactly that a uniformly continuous map is continuous in the respective uniform topologies; the item supplies the standard ball proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"lem-metric-uniformity-dictionary","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the metric entourages, induced metric topology, separation, and epsilon-delta interpretation. The item packages these clauses. Unlike the source convention, the library permits an empty metric carrier while requiring filters proper; this creates the empty-carrier defect escalated in A3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"def-uniform-cover-space","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Encyclopedia of Mathematics gives the uniform-cover axioms and Wodzicki develops the associated cover relation. The item uses an equivalent star-refinement presentation and currently overstates equivalence on the empty carrier under the library proper-filter convention.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the standard equivalence between entourage and uniform-cover formulations. The item spells out both constructions; its cover-to-entourage direction needs the nonempty-carrier qualification recorded for A3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"def-gauge-of-pseudometrics","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources define a uniformity from finite intersections of pseudometric balls. The item calls the family a gauge and bundles topology and uniform-continuity clauses; under the local proper-filter convention it also needs a nonempty carrier.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"lem-normal-sequences-of-entourages","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Iterated symmetric entourage roots are the standard normal-sequence construction in both sources, but the Statement makes the strictly weaker foundational hypothesis DC explicit and no located source states that same choice-calibrated proposition. It is established, not novel; the recursion proof is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"lem-pseudometric-from-a-normal-entourage-sequence","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"Both sources state the normal-sequence metrization lemma with the same dyadic control inclusions and path-infimum pseudometric construction. The proof is a notation-adjusted expansion.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
