+          "id": "step-1.2",
+          "claim": "Conversely, let $X$ be Tychonoff. For $x\\ne y$, the singleton $\\{y\\}$ is closed by $T_1$, and complete regularity gives a continuous $f:X\\to[0,1]$ with $f(x)=1$ and $f(y)=0$. Thus the gauge in [L4] has an entourage excluding $(x,y)$, so its intersection is the diagonal and it is separated. It induces the original topology by [L4]. [L3, L4]",
