+    "ex-additive-group-uniformity-on-r": {
+      "citations": [
+        {
+          "fact": "L1",
+          "source": "def-left-and-right-uniformities-of-a-topological-group",
+          "source_section": "Definition",
+          "quote": "The filters generated by the $L_U$ and by the $R_U$ are respectively the\n**left uniformity** and the **right uniformity** of $G$. These are uniformities.\nIndeed, finite intersections of identity neighbourhoods refine finite\nintersections of the corresponding relations; the diagonal lies in every\nrelation; $L_U^{-1}=L_{U^{-1}}$ and $R_U^{-1}=R_{U^{-1}}$; and continuity of\nmultiplication at $(e,e)$ gives a neighbourhood $V$ with\n$V\\cdot V\\subseteq U$, whence\n$L_V\\circ L_V\\subseteq L_U$ and $R_V\\circ R_V\\subseteq R_U$.\nThus all axioms of [[def-uniform-space-by-entourages]] hold.",
+          "uses": [
+            "1.1"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
+          "fact": "L1",
+          "source": "def-group",
+          "source_section": "Definition",
+          "quote": "A **group** is a monoid $(G,*,e)$ ([[def-semigroup-and-monoid]]) in which every\nelement is invertible ([[def-invertible-element]]). Written out, a group is a set\n$G$ with a binary operation $*$ ([[def-binary-operation]]) and an element\n$e \\in G$ such that",
+          "uses": [
+            "1.1"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
+          "fact": "L2",
+          "source": "def-upper-and-roelcke-uniformities-of-a-topological-group",
+          "source_section": "Definition",
+          "quote": "For the Roelcke structure, left and right relations commute:\n$L_U\\circ R_V=R_V\\circ L_U$, both saying that $y\\in VxU$. Their inverses are\nagain such composites, and if $U_0^{\\,2}\\subseteq U$ and\n$V_0^{\\,2}\\subseteq V$, then\n$$(L_{U_0}\\circ R_{V_0})^{\\circ2}\\subseteq L_U\\circ R_V.$$\nFinite intersections are refined by intersecting the identity\nneighbourhoods. Hence both displayed bases satisfy\n[[def-uniform-space-by-entourages]]. The names and formulas are kept separate.",
+          "uses": [
