+{"id":"lem-topological-group-translations-and-inversion","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"The BIU notes state that left and right shifts and inversion are homeomorphisms. The proof expands continuity and inverse formulas.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
+{"id":"def-left-and-right-uniformities-of-a-topological-group","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. BIU gives exactly these entourage formulas under an explicit Hausdorff hypothesis, while the item correctly defines them for arbitrary, possibly non-Hausdorff topological groups. Dropping Hausdorff is standard established mathematics, but it is a genuine hypothesis delta and no matching source surfaced.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
