+          "id": "step-2.1",
+          "claim": "The family $(E_\\varepsilon)_{\\varepsilon>0}$ is nonempty, omits the empty set, and is downward directed by step 1.1, so [L4] makes its upward closure a filter. The diagonal, inverse, and square-root properties in step 1.1 then make it a uniformity. Its $E_\\varepsilon[x]$ are precisely metric balls, so its induced topology is the metric topology by [L2] and [L5]. [step 1.1, L2, L4, L5]",
+          "step": "2.1",
