+        {
+          "id": "step-2.1",
+          "claim": "Every $\\mathcal F$ is $\\widehat E$-close to itself: choose an $E$-small member of the Cauchy filter and use it on both sides. The relation $\\widehat E$ is symmetric. If $\\widehat E$ and $\\widehat D$ have respective witnesses $A\\times B$ and $C\\times K$, then $(A\\cap C)\\times(B\\cap K)\\subseteq E\\cap D$, so finite intersections are refined by the corresponding hatted intersection. [step 1.1]",
+          "step": "2.1",
+          "inputs": [
+            "1.1"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "step-2.2",
+          "claim": "Choose a symmetric entourage $D$ with $D^{\\circ2}\\subseteq E$. If $\\mathcal F\\,\\widehat D\\,\\mathcal G$ via $A\\times B\\subseteq D$ and $\\mathcal G\\,\\widehat D\\,\\mathcal H$ via $C\\times K\\subseteq D$, choose $b\\in B\\cap C$. Then $aDbDk$ for every $a\\in A,k\\in K$, so $A\\times K\\subseteq D^{\\circ2}\\subseteq E$. Hence $\\widehat D\\circ\\widehat D\\subseteq\\widehat E$. [step 1.1, L2, choose]",
+          "step": "2.2",
