items/ex-subring-that-is-not-a-subfield.md:64:[L4] Cancellation in the additive group of $\mathbb{Q}$; and, in a field, $x \cdot x = x$ with $x \ne 0$ forces $x = 1$, since multiplying by $x^{-1}$ gives $x = 1$ ([[def-field]], [[lem-field-is-a-commutative-ring]], [[lem-group-cancellation]]).
