+          "source": "lem-metric-uniformity-dictionary",
+          "source_section": "Statement",
+          "quote": "For a metric space $(X,d)$, the sets $E_\\varepsilon=\\{(x,y):d(x,y)<\\varepsilon\\}$, $\\varepsilon>0$, generate a separated uniformity. Its induced topology is the metric topology, and uniform continuity to another metric uniformity is exactly metric uniform continuity.",
