+    "thm-topological-group-uniformities-induce-the-given-topology": {
+      "citations": [
+        {
+          "fact": "L1",
+          "source": "def-left-and-right-uniformities-of-a-topological-group",
+          "source_section": "Definition",
+          "quote": "The filters generated by the $L_U$ and by the $R_U$ are respectively the\n**left uniformity** and the **right uniformity** of $G$. These are uniformities.\nIndeed, finite intersections of identity neighbourhoods refine finite\nintersections of the corresponding relations; the diagonal lies in every\nrelation; $L_U^{-1}=L_{U^{-1}}$ and $R_U^{-1}=R_{U^{-1}}$; and continuity of\nmultiplication at $(e,e)$ gives a neighbourhood $V$ with\n$V\\cdot V\\subseteq U$, whence\n$L_V\\circ L_V\\subseteq L_U$ and $R_V\\circ R_V\\subseteq R_U$.\nThus all axioms of [[def-uniform-space-by-entourages]] hold.",
+          "uses": [
+            "1.1",
+            "1.2",
+            "1.3"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
+          "fact": "L2",
+          "source": "lem-topological-group-translations-and-inversion",
+          "source_section": "Statement",
+          "quote": "For $g$ in a topological group, $L_g(x)=gx$, $R_g(x)=xg$, and $\\iota(x)=x^{-1}$ are homeomorphisms.",
+          "uses": [
+            "1.1",
+            "1.2",
+            "1.3"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
+          "fact": "L3",
+          "source": "thm-uniformity-induces-a-topology",
+          "source_section": "Statement",
+          "quote": "For a uniformity $\\mathcal U$ on $X$, call $O\\subseteq X$ open when every $x\\in O$ has an entourage $E$ with $E[x]\\subseteq O$. These open sets form a topology on $X$. Its neighbourhood filter at $x$ has $\\{E[x]:E\\in\\mathcal U\\}$ as a base.",
+          "uses": [
+            "1.1",
+            "1.2"
+          ]
+        }
+      ],
+      "derivations": [
+        {
+          "id": "step-1.1",
+          "claim": "As $U$ ranges over neighbourhoods of $e$, $xU$ ranges over neighbourhoods of $x$ by the left translation homeomorphism, so left balls induce the given topology. [L1, L2, L3]",
+          "step": "1.1",
+          "inputs": [
+            "L1",
+            "L2",
+            "L3"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "step-1.2",
+          "claim": "Similarly $Ux$ ranges over neighbourhoods of $x$ by right translation, so right balls induce the given topology. [L1, L2, L3]",
+          "step": "1.2",
+          "inputs": [
