+          "id": "step-2.1",
+          "claim": "Every $\\mathcal F$ is $\\widehat E$-close to itself: choose an $E$-small member of the Cauchy filter and use it on both sides. The relation $\\widehat E$ is symmetric. If $\\widehat E$ and $\\widehat D$ have respective witnesses $A\\times B$ and $C\\times K$, then $(A\\cap C)\\times(B\\cap K)\\subseteq E\\cap D$, so finite intersections are refined by the corresponding hatted intersection. [step 1.1]",
